{"type":"assistant","uuid":"88e51680-da7e-47b8-a85a-6f5bf6249da8","session_id":"36804ae0-7c81-4eac-a0d6-8efb94a491de","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"88e51680-da7e-47b8-a85a-6f5bf6249da8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the SeekArc is defined without an explicit `seekarc:max` attribute. Let me check what the default max value is for the SeekArc library from the triggertrap library.\n\nThe SeekArc widget uses `app:progressColor`, `seekarc:rotation`, `seekarc:startAngle`, and `seekarc:sweepAngle` but doesn't set `seekarc:max`.\n\nThe default max value for SeekArc from triggertrap is typically 100.\n\nNow let me trace through the bug scenario again:\n\n1. User drags Servo 1 to 100 → SeekArc progress becomes 100 (max)\n\n\n2. `onProgressChanged` fires with i=100, display = `(int)(100 * 3.6)` = 360\n3. User taps in circle, keyboard opens\n4. User enters \"38\", taps Enter\n5. `processDegreeInput(degreeText1, seekArc1)` is called\n6. `degree = 38`\n7. `seekArc.setProgress((int)(38/3.6))` = `seekArc.setProgress(10)` (since 38/3.6 = 10.555..., truncated to 10)\n8. `editEnter = true`\n9. SeekArc fires `onProgressChanged` with i=10\n10. `if (editEnter)` is true → `degreeText.setText(String.valueOf(degree))` → displays \"38\"\n\nThis should display \"38\" correctly, so the issue must be that the SeekArc callback fires before `editEnter` gets set, or the flag is somehow reset. Let me check the order of operations—`setProgress(10)` is called first, which triggers the callback, then `editEnter = true` is set, so the callback fires before the flag is actually true. So `editEnter` is set to true after `setProgress()` triggers the callback with the new progress value, which means when `onProgressChanged` fires with i=10, the flag is already true and it displays the entered degree correctly. But if the display shows 36 instead of 38, either `editEnter` wasn't true when the callback fired, or there's another callback invocation I'm missing.\n\nWait—what if `setProgress()` fires the callback with the old progress value before updating to the new one? That would mean the callback fires with i=100 from when the user dragged to 100, `editEnter` is still false, so it displays `100 * 3.6 = 360` instead of the entered 38, then updates the progress to 10.\n\nBut that doesn't explain why we'd see 36 either. Let me reconsider: maybe `setProgress(10)` triggers `onProgressChanged` with i=10, and since `editEnter` is false at that point, it displays `10 * 3.6 = 36` instead of the expected 38. Then later when the user interacts with the text field, the display updates to show the entered value. The real issue is that `editEnter` needs to be set to true before calling `setProgress()` so the callback knows to display the entered degree rather than recalculating from the progress value.\n\nSetting `editEnter = true` first prevents the callback from displaying the wrong value when progress changes. But there's still a potential issue: if the SeekArc widget fires multiple callbacks during `setProgress()`, like an initial callback with the old progress value, the second approach would handle that correctly since `editEnter` would already be true for all subsequent callbacks. I'm realizing the order of operations matters here—`setProgress()` triggers the callback before `editEnter` is actually set, so when the callback fires with the new progress value, `editEnter` is still false. That's why it displays 36 instead of preserving the entered value. The fix is to set `editEnter = true` before calling `setProgress()`.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
