{"type":"assistant","uuid":"0931591e-a596-4e2b-965c-7b9bbc9745e9","session_id":"36804ae0-7c81-4eac-a0d6-8efb94a491de","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"0931591e-a596-4e2b-965c-7b9bbc9745e9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nHere is the complete bug fix:\n\n## Bug: Robotic Arm — rounding error when entering values with keyboard\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/io/pslab/activity/RoboticArmActivity.java`\n\n**Root cause:** In `processDegreeInput()`, the `seekArc.setProgress()` call fires the `onProgressChanged` callback *before* `editEnter` is set to `true`. When the user enters \"38\", the SeekArc progress becomes `(int)(38/3.6) = 10`, and the callback computes `(int)(10 * 3.6) = 36` instead of using the entered value.\n\n**Fix:** Move `editEnter = true` before `seekArc.setProgress()`.\n\n```diff\n     if (degree > 360 || degree < 0) {\n         degreeText.setText(getResources().getString(R.string.zero));\n         seekArc.setProgress(0);\n         toastInvalidValueMessage();\n     } else {\n-        seekArc.setProgress((int) (degree / 3.6));\n         editEnter = true;\n+        seekArc.setProgress((int) (degree / 3.6));\n     }\n```\n\n**Before (buggy):** `setProgress()` fires callback → callback sees `editEnter=false` → displays `36`\n\n**After (fixed):** `editEnter=true` → `setProgress()` fires callback → callback sees `editEnter=true` → displays `degree` (the original \"38\")"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45650,"output_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":44016,"total_tokens":46023}}}
